From 8747f59cf25998d0fede204a19c799e216d111b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:59:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 67/74] Song browser: a file known by its name across folder
 reads; typed names load

The steps over a folded group, BACK's walk to the group's first version and
the check whether a turn got anywhere compared numFileItemsDeletedAtStart
plus the index across reads of the folder. That isn't where a file is: a
read that culls the window's start drops one more file than it counts
(deleteFolderAndDuplicateItems()). After a one-step move across such a
read (BACK from a group's second version at the window's start)
selectGroupTop() saw "not moved" and kept the previous version's name in
enteredText, which the selected row shows, which names the song LOAD loads
and which delete unlinks: F 1's file loaded as "F 2". The file is now
compared by its name.

Typing: a group's first version typed exactly (the row shows the name
typed, no arrow) folded the group out when pressed; now a typed name loads
(qwertyVisible or arrived at by typing, on both displays; BACK folding a
group in ends that). BACK after typing onto a later version at the window's
first item didn't see it as one (the file before it isn't in the window)
and left the browser; the window is now read back from it first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
